<title>GERMANY: Berlin - Rubin says U.S. believes in strong dollar.</title>
<headline>Berlin - Rubin says U.S. believes in strong dollar.</headline>
<dateline>BERLIN 1997-02-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin said on Saturday that a strong dollar is in the interest of the United States and suggested developments in the Japanese economy beared watching.</p>
<p>&quot;A strong dollar is (in) the U.S. interest. We have had a strong dollar for some time now,&quot; Rubin told a news conference after the G7 meeting of leading industrial nations.</p>
<p>Rubin declined to offer any thoughts on how exchange rate developments would be monitored and refused to comment on the possibility of exchange rate intervention.</p>
</text>
